sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Admin as Admin / OLM
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant API as kube-apiserver<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS1.2+
    participant Op as openshift-kueue-operator<br/>SA token
    participant CM as cert-manager
    participant WH as kueue-webhook-service<br/>443→9443/TCP HTTPS
    participant KCM as kueue-controller-manager<br/>9443 webhook / 8443 metrics
    participant Prom as prometheus-k8s<br/>openshift-monitoring

    Note over Admin,KCM: Flow 1 - Operator reconciliation
    Admin->>API: Create Kueue "cluster" (6443/TCP HTTPS)<br/>Auth: User token
    API-->>Op: Watch event on Kueue CR
    Op->>API: Discovery: cert-manager.io/v1 Issuer?<br/>SA token (hard gate, abort if missing)
    Op->>API: Apply Issuer, Certificates, ConfigMap, RBAC,<br/>Services, CRDs, NetworkPolicies, webhooks,<br/>ServiceMonitor, Deployment (SA token)
    CM->>API: Write TLS Secrets kueue-webhook-server-cert,<br/>metrics-server-cert, inject CA bundle (cert-manager SA)
    API-->>KCM: Operand pods start (2 replicas, leader election)
    Op->>API: Update Kueue status conditions

    Note over User,KCM: Flow 2 - Workload admission (namespace labelled kueue.openshift.io/managed=true)
    User->>API: Create Job/PyTorchJob/RayJob<br/>label kueue.x-k8s.io/queue-name<br/>Auth: User token
    API->>WH: AdmissionReview POST /mutate-*, /validate-*<br/>443→9443/TCP HTTPS, cert-manager CA<br/>NetworkPolicy: openshift-kube-apiserver only
    WH->>KCM: Forward to 9443
    KCM-->>API: Admission response (defaulted, suspended)
    API-->>User: Created (suspended)
    KCM->>API: Create Workload, check ClusterQueue quota,<br/>unsuspend job when admitted (SA token)

    Note over Prom,KCM: Flow 3 - Metrics
    Prom->>KCM: GET /metrics 8443/TCP HTTPS<br/>TLS verified, serverName pinned<br/>Bearer token + client cert
    KCM->>API: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview
    API-->>KCM: Allowed (kueue-metrics-reader)
    KCM-->>Prom: Prometheus metrics
